<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan buys July N+A naphtha at around $215/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan buys July N+A naphtha at around $215/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has bought by tender 28,000 tonnes of July naphthenic and aromatic (N+A) naphtha at slightly above $215 per tonne cost-and-freight (c-and-f) Kaohsiung, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The tender which sought the cargo for July 20-31 arrival, closed May 28 and was valid for two days.</p>
<p>The award was much lower than CPC's last tender, for May 11-31 delivery, which was awarded at just below $230 per tonne, c-and-f.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
